{
 "decisions": {
  "expeditions": "server/src/expeditions.ts + expeditionsApi.ts are the persistence of the Obstaculos campaign (atomic JSON file per expedition under data/expeditions + the /api/expeditions HTTP API); they import @party/shared/obstaculos/campaign only. Owner = Obstaculos: games/obstaculos/server/ (with their test and crash-writer). apps/server/src/server.ts mounts them. Not in platform/server because platform must not import a game.",
  "purity": "render.ts (HTML strings from icons and HowTo: no DOM API), floor.ts (floor items of the Pizzas sim) and teams.ts (team/roster logic) have no DOM, Node or Phaser; all three are pure. render.ts and teams.ts go to platform/core (the plan tree; render has no Pizzas import, teams imports assist.ts and games.ts), floor.ts goes to games/pizzas/sim (only the Pizzas sim imports it, it types against Game).",
  "npm-names": "before: @party/shared, screen, controller, server, latency-report. after: @pichi/core, @pichi/screen-kit, @pichi/controller-kit, @pichi/server-kit, @pichi/game-pizzas, @pichi/game-obstaculos, @pichi/app-screen, @pichi/app-controller, @pichi/app-server, @pichi/latency-report. tools/*.ts and tools/meta are loose scripts, not packages.",
  "simulation": "The simulation runs on the screen (screen/src/main.ts imports createGame/tick from shared/overcooked and the Obstaculos session); server/src/relay.ts is a relay that only imports protocol (shared) and never calls tick. Sim code therefore lives in games/*/sim and platform/core, never in platform/server.",
  "server-runtime": "The server runs with tsx from source (npm run dev/start: tsx apps/server/src/main.ts) and resolves the workspace packages through node_modules/@pichi/* and their package.json exports to .ts sources, exactly as it resolved @party/shared/* before. It is not compiled to dist. Checked in the F3 gate: the server starts on :5600 and answers /screen/, /c/ and /api/info.",
  "classification": "shared/ files: imported by both games (obstaculos code and Pizzas code) -> platform/core: protocol, difficulty, events (the Emitter), rng; named platform in the plan tree: games (registry), icons, render, stats, lobby/{vote,captain,teams}. Everything else in shared/*.ts is imported only by Pizzas code -> games/pizzas/sim. screen/src/art: fx, gfx, tokens, chef, chefdraw are imported by the Obstaculos renderer -> platform/screen/src/art; screen/src/audio: mixer, synth (+ recipes, music, their dependencies) -> platform/screen/src/audio; the rest of art/audio, scene.ts and tutorial/ are Pizzas-only -> games/pizzas/screen.",
  "known-violations": "A mechanical move leaves platform -> game imports that F4/F5 must cut (all rules stay \"warn\"): core/protocol imports maps, puestos, versus*, obstaculos sim/campaign; core/teams imports assist; core/events imports Pizzas types; core/games imports sabotage-config; screen-kit chef imports Pizzas food. See docs/refactor/depcruise-report.md.",
  "barrels": "platform/core/src/index.ts = export * from ./protocol (the old @party/shared main entry); games/pizzas/sim/index.ts = export * from ./overcooked (the old @party/shared/game entry). Cross-package imports of those two files go through the index; every other cross-package import uses the file path through the package exports pattern, so module evaluation order is the one of today (core and Pizzas import each other, a barrel of everything would create runtime cycles).",
  "folders": "obstaculos keeps its own layout: shared/games/obstaculos/** -> games/obstaculos/** verbatim (root index.ts is the package main, sim/ campaign/ validator/ levels/ generate/ modules/ metric/ stay). Pizzas: flat games/pizzas/sim/ plus versus/ (versus*.ts), school/ (tutorial), recipes/, feel/; golden bots + golden tests in games/pizzas/test/golden, JSON in test/golden/fixtures.",
  "arena": "Not created: the game contract does not exist until F4a, so a manifest would be invented logic. Left for F6.",
  "tests": "Tests move next to their subject (same basename), else to the package of the majority of their imports. events.test.ts and events.mirror.slow.test.ts drive the Pizzas sim, so they go to games/pizzas/sim. apps/server/test holds the websocket tests that start the whole server."
 },
